  <h1>Mathematical Foundations of Neuroscience &amp; Provably Safe Neural Co-Processors</h1>
  <p class="lead">Biological nervous systems are not metaphors for computation — they are literal physical instances of partially observed, mutually adapting, boundary-reshaping systems. Hyperactivity's checked <code>neuro/</code> library develops end-to-end mathematical foundations for neuroscience and brain–computer interfaces: from output-null fibers and symbolic Sum-of-Squares stability certificates over \(\mathbb{Q}\) to proof-gated neural interfaces, cognitive inhibition, and synthetic synesthesia.</p>

